{"classification":"source-typographical-intrusion","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0229","provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH25-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The final 'a' in 'measurea' is a stray character; removing it restores ordinary grammatical prose without changing the mathematical claim.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt256.tex:82","source_text":"sets of finite measurea covering $\\BbbR^r$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt256.tex:82","target_text":"himpunan dengan ukuran berhingga yang menutupi $\\BbbR^r$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S256"}
{"classification":"mathematical-stale-symbol","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0230","math_ordinal":117,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH25-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Part 256C(a)(iii) defines the Borel set H and proves H subset E with negligible difference; E_1 belongs to the preceding subpart and is unavailable here.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt256.tex:163","source_normalized_sha256":"278b781c7f5786553d4272a753cb1ee4260aec449bedce21763945ba26027ad0","source_text":"$\\nu_0E_1=\\nu E$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt256.tex:163","target_normalized_sha256":"096d49cadcc10b3d05361ea26bd687a499e87728334e0872a6d675c6e7837021","target_text":"$\\nu_0H=\\nu E$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S256"}
{"classification":"mathematical-symbol-collision","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0231","provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH25-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Sigma is already bound to the domain of nu. A distinct auxiliary family is necessary to avoid circularity while proving closure and then returning to the original measure domain. Grouped math ordinals 135, 203, 207, 208, 212, 214, 218, 219 and 220 are sealed in the unit QA.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt256.tex:181;254-274","source_text":"reuse of $\\Sigma$ for the auxiliary family in 256C(c)-(e)","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt256.tex:181;254-272","target_text":"fresh auxiliary family $\\Cal C$ used through 256C(d) and early 256C(e); original domain $\\Sigma$ retained at line 274","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S256"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-ambient-space","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0232","provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH25-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The theorem fixes arbitrary dimension r; the closed-set exhaustion and auxiliary sigma-algebra argument must remain in the ambient Euclidean space R^r. Grouped math ordinals 156, 159 and 204 are sealed in the unit QA.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt256.tex:199;201;254","source_text":"three occurrences of $\\Bbb R$ inside the proof for arbitrary $\\BbbR^r$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt256.tex:199;201;254","target_text":"$\\Bbb R^r$ restored at all three occurrences","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S256"}
